.SS [utilities]
The utilities panel (`[utilities]`): the quick toggles it lists, and in which order.
.sp
`toggles` is a list of ids rather than a switch per toggle, because the order is the point \(em the toggles a user reaches for live at the front. An id this build does not have holds its place in the grid as a tile saying so, rather than failing the config \(em a name from a newer build costs one tile instead of the whole panel \(em and is reported by `hogar\-shell config check` and in the notice the running shell keeps up while a problem lasts.
.TP
.B columns
How many columns the toggle grid uses.
.sp
Default: \fB4\fR
.TP
.B show_capture
Show the capture (screenshot / recorder) card under the toggles.
.sp
Default: \fBtrue\fR
